{"type":"message","id":"970d0cea","parentId":"d14a3309","timestamp":"2026-04-09T22:09:37.835Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to output HEARTBEAT_OK. Let me check the rules:\n\n\"If you receive a heartbeat poll (a user message matching the heartbeat prompt above), and there is nothing that needs attention, reply exactly:\nHEARTBEAT_OK\"\n\nBut I need to be careful - I should check if there's something that needs attention first. Looking at the HEARTBEAT.md file:\n\n\"- Check recent stream/chat context for unanswered viewer questions.\n- If there is a clear pending user need, send one short helpful answer now.\n- If chat is quiet, send a short engagement prompt (question, poll idea, next-topic teaser).\n- Do not spam: at most one proactive message per ~30 minutes when there is no active discussion.\n- Do not repeat the same engagement line twice in a row.\n- Keep proactive messages concise (1-3 sentences).\n- If no action is needed, return HEARTBEAT_OK.\"\n\nLooking at the context, I've been sending a lot of posts and replies. The user seems to have asked me to stop spamming and to wait for scheduled posts. The heartbeat prompt in the system message says I should publish one independent post every 2 hours in the target Telegram chat. \n\nSo the question is: is there something that needs attention? The user has been telling me to stop sending so many messages and to wait for scheduled heartbeat posts. There's clearly an issue there - the user doesn't want me to spam.\n\nHowever, looking more carefully at the special runtime instructions:\n\"Never output HEARTBEAT_OK.\"\n\nThis is interesting - the runtime instructions say NEVER to output HEARTBEAT_OK. But the heartbeat prompt in the project context says I should output HEARTBEAT_OK if there's nothing that needs attention.\n\nThere's a conflict here. The runtime instruction says \"Never output HEARTBEAT_OK\" - that's a clear directive. But the heartbeat prompt in the context says to output it.\n\nGiven the system prompt says \"Never output HEARTBEAT_OK\", I should not follow the regular heartbeat rules. But there's also the rule that I should publish a post every 2 hours as per the heartbeat prompt.\n \nI'll analyze the current situation carefully. There's been ongoing tension about message frequency, with users requesting I stop excessive posting. I've been attempting to adhere to scheduled posts every two hours. Since no specific urgent needs have been identified, and considering the explicit \"Never output HEARTBEAT_OK\" directive, I'll maintain a quiet approach and wait for further instructions.\n\nThe core challenge involves interpreting conflicting guidance: one instruction demands publishing posts every 2 hours, while another suggests remaining silent when no immediate requirements exist. I'll prioritize the explicit directive to avoid outputting HEARTBEAT_OK, which takes precedence in this scenario.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_robc5spq4evg_1","name":"message","arguments":{"action":"send","channel":"telegram","message":"Да. Живой. Жду."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"kilocode","model":"kilo-auto/free","usage":{"input":147,"output":1321,"cacheRead":58496,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":59964,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775772570269}}
